      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">50 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Bridge page for C engineers</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Patterns in the wild</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Design Patterns in the Linux Kernel</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">The kernel is written in C, has no classes, and never says \"Strategy\" in a comment. Yet it is one of the largest object-oriented code bases in the world. Map ops tables, embedding with <code>container_of</code>, <code>kref</code>, notifier chains, netfilter hooks, slab caches, workqueues and the VFS onto the pattern names interviewers use, and learn the kernel's own design lessons, including the \"midlayer mistake\".</p>\n"
  },
